{"input_text": "Question: I have to calculate this 
\begin{align}
& (1-p)^{N-1}+\frac{1}{2}C_{N-1}^{N-2}(1-p)^{N-2}p+\frac{1}{3}C_{N-1}^{N-3}(1-p)^{N-3}p^{2}+...+\frac{1}{N-2}C_{N-1}^{1}(1-p)p^{N-2}\\
& +\frac{1}{N}p^{N-1}
\end{align}
where $C_{n}^{m}=\frac{n!}{m!(n-m)!}$.  
 Can anyone help to sum this up? Thank you.  

Answer: Let $\{y_i^*\}_{i=1}^n$ be the decreasing (i.e., non-increasing) arrangement of the $y_i$'s. $x$ is majorized by $y$ if and only if $a_k=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^ky_i^{*}\geq\frac{1}{n}$ for each $k=1,2,\dots n$. But $a_k$ is non-increasing, as can easily be checked, that is, 
$$a_1\geq a_2\cdots\geq a_n=\frac{1}{n},$$
so the assertion is proved.  
